r/preparation_equivalence_legacy_test.go\": {\n    \"sha256\": \"328bfdec937d16d1771e746818231b33522c58ed9f19214d5978ea99ec61b17e\",\n    \"bytes\": 2187,\n    \"preimage\": \".flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-7/preimages/tools/gomad3/runner/preparation_equivalence_legacy_test.go\",\n    \"provenance\": \"task-7-created baseline probe, captured before later edits; not original Runner source\"\n  },\n  \"tools/gomad3/internal/preparation/preparation_test.go\": {\n    \"sha256\": \"34aecf8ee75b2d42886c1ba8feb0c875f23ad059c82ab8ad9f978b119669aaa2\",\n    \"bytes\": 1846,\n    \"preimage\": \".flow/artifacts/fn-109-gomad-deepen-modules-and-tool-interfaces/task-7/preimages/tools/gomad3/internal/preparation/preparation_test.go\",\n    \"provenance\": \"task-7-created test initial RED version\"\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"frozen_at_utc\": \"2026-10-03T13:50:34.069702+00:00\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"tools/gomad3/architecture_test.go\": \"c02a298b6060dfdde7a77df85d83b3db0c6d112b26fbd5860e27d22658cfd176\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/internal/preparation/preparation.go\": \"c5ff22c09d7c4495b5a3035c47bd8dfde4a6ca5978c1df1b6d5414ed57d749aa\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/internal/preparation/preparation_test.go\": \"cf0ebe99a53f3e1a47e1835b9910fd39c4ca2aaa9dd43cb68d3f6b3b0da0b88f\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/runner/deterministicio.go\": \"f55f752c2611ae6da7519e25223a2c11144cd3495aea2d0fc9abe00e07d54425\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/runner/portable_plan.go\": \"95112a7c797ef8592c7af6b19fd187e3d55f4daef21cbb4b9720ab770d8bd3ee\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/runner/preparation_equivalence_legacy_test.go\": \"0db44bbf2f4c84617d75e8b77ad52df735a6834a02064a4dfc9896400b098404\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/runner/preparation_owner_test.go\": \"e8d0309b038a77217d0d4e011a9430838563468b087be105d6a93ad191a7b66c\",\n    \"tools/gomad3/runner/runner.go\": \"c257c5ee5f299e7b2dc1fec54a42918ec535291c8de67912e949bc6a0c94d2cf\"\n  },\n  \"task_only_patch_sha256\": \"8421c95c2d359130d14664b94181756ee1f8be4035a62eb41d8791c285613cb8\",\n  \"preimages_manifest_sha256\": \"69bd760e751ebf55938e60f424ca6f9bf6ead2341e6d1c86df33f46488403e36\",\n  \"toolchain_key\": \"2ecdbd330bb5928f360739fdd80cb3eb0f0764e513a5cc208cd83714fff0a457\"\n}\n# Task 7 source handover\n\nThe new `internal/preparation` owner selects build adapters, prepares the target, attaches adapter identities, validates the result, and removes its exclusively created adapter workspace. Explore and portable planning call it with their durable preparation roots. Explore retains journal transitions and its existing target-preparer versus adapter/validation error staging. Custom preparers still skip adapter selection and receive an empty nonnil adapter slice. The portable bundle root is now assigned before adapter selection.\n\nThe four actual pre-edit source files and their SHA256 hashes are in `preimages.json`; the two later probe snapshots are explicitly labeled task-created. `task-only.patch` compares those four true originals with final source and treats all four task-created files as additions. `final-source.json` freezes eight source hashes at 2026-10-03T13:50:34Z; all eight matched after the host run. Every original comment line in the touched files remains present (`comments-preserved.json`). No git staging or commit was performed.\n\nFixed-input old protocol and new-owner snapshots are byte equal for both a simple external module and the pinned Sprig adapter, on fresh and cache preparations, after normalizing only `Prepared.Path`. Each snapshot includes complete `target.Prepared` and `RecordTarget` projections. The Sprig identity and binary SHA are stable. The captured old portable caller, run through `legacy-portable-overlay.json`, fails the selected-adapter regression with `deterministic I/O build adapter requires module cache and preparation root`; current source passes. New tests also cover an external module with local replacement, two independent preparations, invalid sums, replacement conflicts, cleanup failure with and without a primary target failure, and custom-preparer workspace preservation. Existing Runner tests pass for changed binaries, cancellation, overall timeout, and preparation journal failure.\n\nScoped vet, architecture/exact-edge/public API and external consumer checks, task-only lint (`0 issues`), and a final-source CLI build passed. The full `test-host` log has 46 `ok` package results and no `FAIL` or make error. Its wrapper exited 1 **after** the package output because it assigned zsh's read-only `status` variable while recording exit metadata. The underlying make exit was not captured; the raw log, exact wrapper script, terminal tool receipt, CLI binary hash, commands, observed exits and log hashes are in `handover.json`. The pre-edit broad baseline also exited 1 on `watchdog_absent` in Runner execution; its exact selector passed on retry. That original baseline output is in the tool transcript (session 15260, chunk fe3611), without an on-disk raw log. Native Linux qualification remains unavailable on this darwin/arm64 host.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
